I've pushed my changes to feature/fvar_operands_and_partials. I've added a single test for normal at src/test/agrad/fwd/prob/univariate/continuous/normal_test.cpp.

I think the right thing to do is to extend the testing framework to generate every valid combination of tests. For normal_log, that means each of the 3 arguments can be:
1. double
2. var
3. fvar<double>
4. vector<double>
5. vector<var>
6. vector<fvar<double> >
7. Eigen::Matrix<double, 1, -1> (row_vector)
8. Eigen::Matrix<var, 1, -1> (row_vector)
9. Eigen::Matrix<fvar<double>, 1, -1> (row_vector)
10. Eigen::Matrix<double, -1, 1> (vector)
11. Eigen::Matrix<var, -1, 1> (vector)
12. Eigen::Matrix<fvar<double>, -1, 1> (vector)

Except, we won't have all 12^3 combinations. If I understood the induction arguments correctly, we can't have fvar<double> and var in the same argument list.

Should we add fvar<var> in there too? That's going to get complicated.

