> Honestly, it almost looks like someone hardcoded two digits in the exponent in the stringstream code.

But

   ss << "2.22507e-308";
   ss >> y;
   std::cout << "y=" << y << std::endl;

prints

   y=0

whereas using

   ss << "2.22508e-308";

prints

   y=2.22508e-308

so it looks like it's just numbers less than numeric_limits<double>::min()
and greater than numeric_limits<double>::denorm_min().  Recall:

   min=2.22507e-308
   denorm min=4.94066e-324

