Precision is number of digits past the decimal place in the selected format.  So, yes, there is more information displayed in scientific notation but (a) it would look awkward if the mantissas didn't match and (b) there would be inconsistent formatting if a column had a number much larger than 1 and one less than one (for example 111 and 0.1.

